    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 6104 closed 2022 with opening gross claims outstanding of $110.335m (2021), reducing to $64.038m at 31 Dec 2022. The syndicate booked an over-provision in respect of prior claims of $12.195m (gross) in 2022, recorded as favourable prior-year development (a release). Management attributes prior-year reserve releases in part to favourable prior-year catastrophe development (notably Typhoon Faxai, Typhoon Hagibis, Typhoon Jebi, Hurricane Ida and US tornadoes) together with gradual release of held reserving margin as estimates matured; the syndicate continues to hold specific reserves for COVID-19 exposures (circa $18.7m).",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "prior-year catastrophe reserve releases for events such as Typhoons Faxai, Hagibis and Jebi, Hurricane Ida, and US tornadoes",
      "Booked reserves include a net margin of $23.2 million (2021: $27.2 million), representing 31.7% (2021: 28.3%) of net booked reserves. This is the margin above the best estimate to help mitigate the uncertainty within the reserve estimates. As the best estimate matures and becomes more certain, the management margin is gradually released.",
      "The Syndicate has material exposure to losses arising out of the Covid-19 pandemic and currently reserves $18.7 million (2021: $20.4 million) for these claims."
    ],
